LiteX (https://github.com/enjoy-digital/litex)

MIRLO64 is not a LiteX system and is not built with LiteX. Three files derive
from LiteX's code and are used under its BSD 2-Clause License:

* rtl/soc/sdr_phy.sv: the SDRAM PHY, a port to SystemVerilog of LiteX's
  half-rate generic SDR PHY as openfpga-litex adapted it to the Pocket;
* rtl/soc/jtag_uart_bridge.v: generated from LiteX's AlteraJTAG and JTAGPHY
  (the JTAG UART, which the released bitstream leaves out);
* tools/jtag/sfl_term.py: LiteX's litex_term.py with changes for the Pocket's
  JTAG UART relay (the header in the file names its authors).

The boot ROM (lang/mips/boot) implements LiteX's SFL serial-boot protocol, and
lang/mips/include (uart.h, console.h, irq.h, system.h) declares the interfaces
of LiteX's libbase; they are covered by this notice for that reason.

